IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`
IMPORT `sgc2-sch13-small`
IMPORT `sgc2-s205a-exemption`

-- Tests for sgc2-s205a-exemption.l4 (sections 205A, 205B, 205C and 205D). Every expected value is written from the text of the sections, beside the assertion, not from the code.
-- A date is Date day month year. Argument order is the order of the GIVEN lines of the function under test.

§ `Transactions used in the tests`

-- A transaction is: its record is required under section 199(1); then the matters (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (fa) of section 205B(3); then the nominal-sum flag (fb), the sum, the most that may be prescribed; then (g).
`a sale of goods` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`a subscriber takes shares` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`the appointment of the secretary` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`the appointment of an auditor` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`the upkeep of the registered office` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`the keeping of the registers` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`the payment of a filing fee` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`the payment of a composition amount` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
`a nominal receipt of 50 where the most prescribed is 100` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 50, 100, FALSE
`a nominal receipt of 100 where the most prescribed is 100` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 100, 100, FALSE
`a nominal receipt of 101 where the most prescribed is 100` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 101, 100, FALSE
`a prescribed matter` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, TRUE
`a happening whose record is not required` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE

-- Years of the Thirteenth Schedule, for the one assertion that feeds section 205C(5) from the Schedule: revenue, total assets, employees (ceilings $10,000,000, $10,000,000 and 50).
`a year with revenue and total assets at the ceilings and 51 employees` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 10000000, 51
`a year with revenue at the ceiling and the rest over` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 10000001, 51
`a year with every figure over its ceiling` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000001, 10000001, 51

§ `The seam to section 7A(2)`

-- Either answer TRUE gives TRUE; NOTHING or FALSE from both gives FALSE (a plain BOOLEAN seam, as the keel takes it).
#ASSERT `s 205B and 205C the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B and 205C the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B and 205C the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B and 205C the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B and 205C the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 205A(1)`

#ASSERT `s 205A(1) the company and its directors are exempt from section 205(1) or (2)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A company not so exempt: the subsection is silent (a scope limit with no "only"): NOTHING, not FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 205A(1) the company and its directors are exempt from section 205(1) or (2)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 205A(2)`

-- "at any time before the next annual general meeting": the last day is the day before the meeting.
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the last day for the company to appoint an auditor` (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS Date 14 6 2026
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the last day for the company to appoint an auditor` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- Ceased to be exempt, meeting on 15 June 2026. Not yet appointed: on 14 June not yet in default; on 15 June in default.
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 14 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Appointed on 14 June: in time. Appointed on 15 June, the day of the meeting: too late.
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) TRUE (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not ceased to be exempt: the duty does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` FALSE (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The auditors so appointed hold office until the conclusion of the meeting, not after.
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the auditors appointed hold office` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205A(2) the auditors appointed hold office` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Ceased on 1 June 2026, meeting on 15 June: 13 days after the day it ceased (the last day is 14 June).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 205A(2) the company must appoint an auditor before the next annual general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 205A(2) appoint a person or persons to be auditor or auditors of the company` AT 13

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 205A(2) the company must appoint an auditor before the next annual general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 205A(2) appoint a person or persons to be auditor or auditors of the company` AT 14

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 205A(2) the company must appoint an auditor before the next annual general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 14)

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 205A(2) the company must appoint an auditor before the next annual general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 13)

§ `Section 205A(3)`

#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The text makes only the company and the directors in default guilty.
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE `s 205(17) any other person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No default in complying with subsection (2): no offence.
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` FALSE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` FALSE `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The fine: not exceeding $5,000, for those made guilty; the text states no penalty for anyone else.
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` TRUE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` TRUE `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` TRUE `s 205(17) any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 205A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` FALSE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 205B(1)`

#ASSERT `s 205B(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither limb: the "if" is not met (marginal reading, NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 205B(2): dormancy`

-- No transaction at all: dormant.
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A transaction whose record section 199(1) does not require is not an accounting transaction.
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `a happening whose record is not required`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An accounting transaction that subsection (3) does not disregard ends dormancy.
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `a sale of goods`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An accounting transaction subsection (3) disregards does not.
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `the payment of a filing fee`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `the payment of a filing fee`, `the appointment of an auditor`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One disregarded and one not: the one not disregarded counts, in either order.
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `the payment of a filing fee`, `a sale of goods`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `a sale of goods`, `the payment of a filing fee`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A nominal receipt above the prescribed most is not disregarded.
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `a nominal receipt of 101 where the most prescribed is 100`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` (LIST `a nominal receipt of 100 where the most prescribed is 100`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "the company ceases to be dormant on the occurrence of such a transaction".
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company ceases to be dormant on the transaction` `a sale of goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company ceases to be dormant on the transaction` `the payment of a filing fee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(2) the company ceases to be dormant on the transaction` `a happening whose record is not required` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 205B(3): the transactions to be disregarded`

-- Each of (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (fa), (g) in turn.
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `a subscriber takes shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `the appointment of the secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `the appointment of an auditor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `the upkeep of the registered office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `the keeping of the registers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `the payment of a filing fee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `the payment of a composition amount` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `a prescribed matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (fb): a nominal sum not exceeding the prescribed amount, on both sides of it.
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `a nominal receipt of 50 where the most prescribed is 100` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `a nominal receipt of 100 where the most prescribed is 100` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Over the prescribed amount, and a transaction arising from none of the matters: the list is not closed with "only", so the text says nothing: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `a nominal receipt of 101 where the most prescribed is 100` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` `a sale of goods` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 205B(4)`

-- (a), (b), (c): each applies where the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt under (1); where it is not, JUST FALSE ("where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)).
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(a) the copies of the financial statements to be sent under section 203 need not be audited` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(a) the copies of the financial statements to be sent under section 203 need not be audited` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(b) section 203 has effect with the omission of any reference to the auditor's report or a copy of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(b) section 203 has effect with the omission of any reference to the auditor's report or a copy of it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(c) copies of an auditor's report need not be laid before the company in a general meeting` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(c) copies of an auditor's report need not be laid before the company in a general meeting` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d): the directors are in default unless the return is accompanied by a statement saying all three things.
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not exempt at the end of the year: the duty does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The text states no time and no consequence for (d): a trace can be fulfilled or left open, and never reaches breach (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 205B(4)(d) the directors must accompany the annual return with a statement` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Ann" DOES `s 205B(4)(d) accompany the annual return with a statement by the directors` AT 5

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 205B(4)(d) the directors must accompany the annual return with a statement` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `Section 205B(5)`

-- Exempt under (1) and ceases to be dormant: thereupon ceases to be exempt.
#ASSERT `s 205B(5) the company ceases to be exempt from audit requirements` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(5) the company ceases to be exempt from audit requirements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205B(5) the company ceases to be exempt from audit requirements` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- It remains exempt for the accounts of the year it was dormant throughout; the text says nothing of another year.
#ASSERT `s 205B(5) the company remains exempt in relation to the accounts for the financial year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(5) the company remains exempt in relation to the accounts for the financial year` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 205B(6)`

-- Financial year 1 January to 31 December 2026: the notice may be given from 1 January 2026 to 30 November 2026 (one month before the end of the year).
-- Arguments: shares, shares held by those giving notice, class shares, class shares held by them, members, members giving notice, in writing, day given, first day, last day.
-- Exactly 5% of the shares (50 of 1,000), in writing, on the last day for notice: in order.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One day late: outside a period the text fixes in its own words: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 1 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The first day of the year is in the period; the day before is not "during a financial year".
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 49 of 1,000 is under 5%: the holding is a named complement of the grant, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 49 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5% of a class: 10 of 200 class shares.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 0 200 10 0 0 TRUE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 0 200 9 0 0 TRUE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5% of the members: 2 of 40, and 1 of 40 is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 0 0 0 40 2 TRUE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 0 0 0 40 1 TRUE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Enough shares, but the notice is not in writing: the text asks for "written notice": NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 FALSE (Date 30 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A year ending on 31 March 2027: one month before has no 31st in February, so the last day for notice is 28 February 2027 (the month clamps); 1 March is late.
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 28 2 2027) (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 31 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` 1000 50 0 0 0 0 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 31 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 205B(7)`

-- Where a notice is given, the company is not entitled to the exemption in (1) for the year: the flat negative.
#ASSERT `s 205B(7) the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Where none is given, the subsection takes nothing away ("where": JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `s 205B(7) the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under section 205B for a year: (1) and (7) together. Dormant from formation, no notice: exempt.
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) and (7) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Dormant since the end of the previous year, no notice: exempt.
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) and (7) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Dormant, but a member gave notice: not entitled.
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) and (7) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not dormant, no notice: not exempt under (1).
#ASSERT `s 205B(1) and (7) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 205B(8)`

#ASSERT `s 205B(8) "accounting transaction" the transaction is an accounting transaction` `a sale of goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(8) "accounting transaction" the transaction is an accounting transaction` `the payment of a filing fee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205B(8) "accounting transaction" the transaction is an accounting transaction` `a happening whose record is not required` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 205C(1) and (6): the small company exempt from the audit`

-- Arguments of (1): small company, parent company, subsidiary company, part of a small group, first day of the financial year.
-- A small company that is neither parent nor subsidiary, in a year from 1 January 2026: exempt.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A year commencing on 1 July 2015 is the first to which the section applies; one commencing on 30 June 2015 is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 7 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 30 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent company that is a small company and part of a small group: exempt; not part of a small group: the text says subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A subsidiary company likewise.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent company that is not a small company: the bar of (3) says no.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company that is not a small company and neither parent nor subsidiary: the subsection says nothing of it (it may be exempt under section 205B).
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (6): the section does not apply to a financial year commencing before 1 July 2015.
#ASSERT `s 205C(6) this section applies to the company for the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(6) this section applies to the company for the financial year` (Date 1 7 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6), second limb: the duty under the earlier Part VI, in default if either part was not done.
#ASSERT `s 205C(6) the company and its directors are in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(6) the company and its directors are in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(6) the company and its directors are in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(6) the company and its directors are in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 205C(2)`

#ASSERT `s 205C(2) section 205B(4), (6) and (7) apply to the small company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(2) section 205B(4), (6) and (7) apply to the small company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 205B(7) as applied: a notice takes the exemption away.
#ASSERT `s 205C(2) the small company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(2) the small company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under section 205C for a year: (1) and (2) together. Small, no notice: exempt; small, notice given: not.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) and (2) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) and (2) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not small and a notice given: subsection (1) gave no exemption to take away; the answer stays NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 205C(1) and (2) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 205C(3) and (4)`

-- A parent company: barred unless it is both a small company and part of a small group.
#ASSERT `s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a parent company: the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A subsidiary company likewise.
#ASSERT `s 205C(4) subsection (1) applies to the company as a subsidiary company` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 205C(4) subsection (1) applies to the company as a subsidiary company` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(4) subsection (1) applies to the company as a subsidiary company` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(4) subsection (1) applies to the company as a subsidiary company` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 205C(5): the meanings come from the Thirteenth Schedule`

#ASSERT `s 205C(5) "small company" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(5) "small company" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(5) "small group" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(5) "small group" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Fed with the Schedule's own answer: a first-year company with revenue and total assets at the ceilings (2 of 3 criteria) is a small company.
#ASSERT `s 205C(5) "small company" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` (`sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 1 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE `a year with revenue and total assets at the ceilings and 51 employees` `a year with every figure over its ceiling` `a year with every figure over its ceiling`) EQUALS TRUE
-- One criterion only: not a small company.
#ASSERT `s 205C(5) "small company" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` (`sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 1 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE `a year with revenue at the ceiling and the rest over` `a year with every figure over its ceiling` `a year with every figure over its ceiling`) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 205C(7)`

-- A company mentioned in (6) that lodged a return without attaching the accounts: in default; with them attached, or no return lodged, or not a company of (6): not.
#ASSERT `s 205C(7) the company is in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205C(7) the company is in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(7) the company is in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205C(7) the company is in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- No time of its own (the deadline for the return is section 197): fulfilled when done, and open otherwise, never in breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 205C(7) the company must attach a copy of the accounts to the return` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 205C(7) attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return lodged under section 197` AT 5

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 205C(7) the company must attach a copy of the accounts to the return` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `Section 205D`

-- The Registrar may require, if satisfied of a breach of section 199 or 201, or that it is otherwise in the public interest, a company exempt under either section.
#ASSERT `s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "if" not met: the grant is not made out (NOTHING, not FALSE).
#ASSERT `s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A company not exempt under section 205B or 205C: the section does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The company's side. Notice given, last day for lodging 31 March 2026. Lodged on the last day: in time. Lodged on 1 April: too late.
#ASSERT `s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not lodged: not yet in default on 31 March, in default on 1 April.
#ASSERT `s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No notice given: no requirement, so no default.
#ASSERT `s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` FALSE (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice given on 1 March 2026 naming 31 March 2026: 30 days.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 205D the company must lodge what the Registrar's notice requires` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 205D lodge the audited financial statements and the auditor's report the Registrar's notice requires` AT 30

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 205D the company must lodge what the Registrar's notice requires` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 205D lodge the audited financial statements and the auditor's report the Registrar's notice requires` AT 31

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 205D the company must lodge what the Registrar's notice requires` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 205D the company must lodge what the Registrar's notice requires` "Acme Pte Ltd" (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)
